          "evidence_id": "assert_passive_radiator",
          "span_id": "span_assert_passive_structure",
          "support_type": "body",
          "text": "A speaker enclosure using a passive radiator usually contains an \"active loudspeaker \" (or main driver), and a passive radiator (also known as a \"drone cone\"). The active loudspeaker is a normal driver, and the passive radiator is of similar construction, but without a voice coil and magnet assembly . It is not attached to a voice coil or wired to an electrical circuit or power amplifier .",
          "text_sha256": "63d41e3769b3e32ce62c90b89e99fce2792fd1c5f189e4d02bedff8ef4a384e6"
        },
        {
          "byte_end": 392,
